; Higher-order binder form — `fold` walks a finite vector while
; threading a running accumulator through each iteration. The body
; `(+ acc x)` re-evaluates once per element with `acc` bound to the
; previous body result and `x` bound to the current element. The
; iteration-0 `acc` is the evaluated `init` (here, `0`). After the
; last element, the form's value is that iteration's body — the
; running sum.
(fold [acc x] 0 [1 2 3 4] (+ acc x))
